        "options": {
          "content": "=INCIDENT TRIAGE REPORT \u2014 AUTOMATED RESPONSE & INTELLIGENCE ANALYST (ARIA)\n================================================================================\n\nINCIDENT METADATA\n-----------------\nIncident ID       : {{ $json.body.incident_id }}\nIncident Title    : {{ $json.body.incident_title }}\nSeverity Level    : {{ $json.body.severity }}\nQueue Timestamp   : {{ $json.body.incident_timestamp }}\nProcessed At      : {{ $json.body.run_timestamp }}\nAnalysis Engine   : ARIA v2.0\nModel Used        : {{ $json.body.model_used }}\n\n================================================================================\n\nROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS\n-------------------\n{{ $json.body.root_cause }}\n\n================================================================================\n\nBUSINESS IMPACT ASSESSMENT\n---------------------------\n{{ $json.body.business_impact }}\n\n================================================================================\n\nRECOMMENDED IMMEDIATE ACTION\n-----------------------------\n{{ $json.body.recommended_action }}\n\n================================================================================\n\nFULL POST-MORTEM REPORT\n------------------------\n{{ $json.body.post_mortem }}\n\n================================================================================\n\nGOVERNANCE TRAIL\n----------------\nThis report was generated automatically by the Automated Incident Response\nSystem (AIRS) v2.0. It has been reviewed by ARIA and passed a 6-field JSON\nschema validation before reaching this document. No manual intervention was\nrequired in the analysis phase.\n\nWorkflow Version  : WF2 - Doc Creation & Escalation Routing\nPipeline          : WF1 \u2192 WF2 \u2192 WF3 (Operational Logs)\nAudit Log Tab     : Run Logs (same Google Sheet as Incident Logs)\n\nThis document is part of an auditable incident governance trail. Do not edit\nthe Governance Trail section \u2014 it is populated automatically.",
          "maxRetries": 3,
          "retryOnFail": true
        }
